# Information and entropy, the count of distinctions a state can hold. The Shannon entropy of a source is the average
# number of bits needed to name its outcome, and for n equally likely outcomes it is the logarithm base two of n, so a
# fair coin holds one bit, a fair four-way choice two bits, a fair eight-way choice three bits. The von Neumann entropy is
# the same measure for a quantum state, the Shannon entropy of its eigenvalues, zero for a pure state and maximal for a
# fully mixed one. Mutual information measures shared uncertainty: the entropy of one part plus the entropy of the other
# minus the entropy of the whole. For a Bell pair, each qubit alone is fully mixed with entropy one, while the pair
# together is pure with entropy zero, so the mutual information is one plus one minus zero, two, the maximum for a single
# qubit on each side. That value two is exactly the wormhole cross-section the holography files measure, twice the
# entanglement entropy of one, and its being positive with a zero joint entropy is the strong subadditivity signature of
# entanglement, the whole knowing less uncertainty than its parts. This file checks the equally-likely entropy, the Bell
# mutual information, its relation to the entanglement entropy, and the subadditivity gap.

# A fair eight-way source holds log base two of eight, three bits, because 2^3 = 8.
hold entropy-of-eight-equally-likely-is-three-bits
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2

# The Bell-pair mutual information: each qubit alone has entropy one, the pair together has entropy zero, so the shared
# information is 1 + 1 - 0 = 2, the maximum for one qubit each.
hold bell-pair-mutual-information-is-two
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call subtract
      call add
        code 1
        code 1
      code 0

# The mutual information is twice the entanglement entropy: the entanglement entropy of the Bell pair is one, and 2 * 1 =
# 2 equals the mutual information, so the cross-section is twice the entropy at the maximum.
hold mutual-information-is-twice-the-entanglement-entropy
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 1

# Subadditivity: the joint entropy zero is below the sum of the parts' entropies two, 0 below 2, the entangled whole
# holding less uncertainty than its parts separately, which is why the mutual information is positive.
hold entanglement-makes-the-whole-less-uncertain-than-its-parts
  call is-below
    code 0
    code 2
